Z||000000||GT Bastard||09-12-2000||02:38 AM||||I was fired from my job today and I had just picked up my things(12 o'clock midnight.) Brad and I pulled up next to a riced-out purple Honda revving at me.  There weren't any other cars around but I declined the race and saved the poor little punk some humiliation.  Just then.... A red two-door Civic pull out with altezza style tail lights and some rims off a VTEC. It actually looked pretty tame until he completely destroyed his tires shifting into second gear...  Sure enough he pulls up next to me at the next red light.  It turns out to be a car built by Excessive Autosports here in Sioux Falls...  The guy that runs it is known for doing Jap motor conversions(and he drives an NSX!)  Anyhow, I asked him what he had and he said, "stock 4-cyl."  I told him I had the Stock 6.  We didn't race off the line, but when I shifted to third he decided to start provoking the almighty Plastic Fiero. We were cruzing side by side down a 4 lane road and I downshifted to second gear and put it the floor.  The Fiero chirped them and launched HARD.  That Honda was right on my ass!  We were dead even all the way through second gear, but he started pulling on me just a little bit in 3rd when we shut down for the next stop.  We pulled over and I talked the guy about the race.  As it turns out, he's running a B16A w/ T3 Turbocharger.  The catch is.... He says it's not tuned yet and it's only running 4lbs of boost.  In any case, the guy was VERY surprised that he couldn't pull on the Fiero in second gear.  He claims that he walked on a C5 early that night!  If we would have raced from a dead stop, I think I could have had him since the Fiero grabs extremely well when his Honda just spins.  The part that really suprised him is that fact that my motor rattles like hell(it's about to throw a rod but the new 3.1 is almost ready to toss in!)  Anyhow, nuff ranting for now.  I would consider that a loss, but it was damn close.  later all...  <P>------------------<BR>Gold 86 SE V6 4-sp w/4.10 gears, Eibach springs, Koni's all around <BR>Yoko's<BR>Coated headers<BR>ACT 4-puck clutch<BR>MSD ignition<BR>Flowmaster w/ mandrel bent 2.5 pipe<BR>extrude honed intake<BR>larger TB<BR>4.10 tranny<BR>Fuel system mods<BR>Prom<p>[This message has been edited by GT Bastard (edited 09-12-2000).]||||reg||4
